  "question": {
    "text": "A wire of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mn>c</mn><mn>m</mn></math>&nbsp;is bent into a semi-circular arc and the two equal halves of the arc are uniformly charged with charges <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>+</mo><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mi>Q</mi></math>&nbsp;as shown in the figure. The magnitude of the charge on each half is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\" separators=\"|\"><mi>Q</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>3</mn></msup><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#949;</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the permittivity of free the space. The net electric field at the centre&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;is<br /><br /><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/b521b243-d9d9-44f2-a518-cbe0a25d5d6d-image.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 141px;\" />",
